<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />

<.page_shell>
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-14 pl-10 sm:pl-12 lg:pt-20 lg:pl-48">
    <p class="text-ink/55 text-label mb-6 font-semibold uppercase lg:absolute lg:top-20 lg:left-0 lg:mb-0 lg:w-32 lg:text-right">
      Privacy
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-hero max-w-3xl font-normal">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-fine text-ink/55 mt-4">Last updated 17 July 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-10 max-w-2xl space-y-8">
      <p class="text-body text-ink/75 font-light">
        Nila is operated by Kaguya Media Private Limited ("Nila", "we", "us").
        This policy explains what we collect, why, who processes it on our
        behalf, and the rights you have over it. It covers
        <span class="font-medium">nila.tax</span>
        and the Nila application. If anything here is unclear, write to <a
          href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax"
          class="text-redink hover:underline"
        >privacy@nila.tax</a>.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Who the data belongs to</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          Our customers are CA firms and accountants. The documents you upload —
          bills, bank statements, GST returns — describe your clients'
          businesses. You are the data fiduciary for that material; Nila is a
          data processor acting on your instructions. We use it only to produce
          the workings you asked for, and never to build a product for anyone
          else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 space-y-2 font-light">
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Account data</span> — name, email, firm
            details, and authentication records for the people who log in.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Uploaded documents</span> — invoices, bank
            statements, GSTR files, photos, and anything else you send Nila to
            process, together with the structured records extracted from them
            (vendors, GSTINs, amounts, tax lines).
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Client and contact details</span> — the
            businesses and people your work concerns, including GSTINs, and the
            phone numbers or emails Nila uses to chase missing documents in your
            firm's name.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Operational logs</span> — audit trails of
            actions taken in the app, and standard technical logs (IP, browser,
            timestamps) needed to run and secure the service.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Why we process it</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          To extract, classify, and draft the GST artifacts you use; to flag the
          lines that need a human; to follow up on missing documents on your
          behalf; to secure the service and keep an audit trail; and to meet our
          legal and tax obligations. We do not sell your data, and we do not use
          your clients' documents for advertising.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Who processes it for us</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We use a small set of sub-processors under contract, each limited to
          what its job needs:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 space-y-2 font-light">
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Hosting</span> — our servers and database
            run on dedicated infrastructure (Hetzner) that we administer.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Document processing / AI</span> — uploaded
            documents may be sent to third-party model providers solely to
            extract and structure their contents for your workings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Email &amp; messaging</span> — transactional
            email (Resend) and messaging providers used to notify you and to
            chase documents.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We will name our current sub-processors on request. Some may process
          data outside India; where they do, we rely on contractual safeguards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We retain documents and the records derived from them for as long as
          your account is active and you need them for your filings, plus the
          period required to meet legal and tax record-keeping obligations. When
          you close your account, we delete or anonymise your data within a
          reasonable period, except where law requires us to keep it longer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">How we protect it</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          Access is scoped per firm — one firm's documents are never served to
          another. Data is encrypted in transit, access is restricted to
          personnel who need it, and sensitive fields such as bank account
          numbers are stored encrypted. No system is perfectly secure, but we
          treat financial documents as sensitive by default.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          You can ask us to access, correct, export, or delete the personal data
          we hold about you, and to address grievances about how we handle it.
          Where you are acting for your clients, we will support you in meeting
          the corresponding requests from them. Write to
          <a href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax" class="text-redink hover:underline">privacy@nila.tax</a>
          and we will respond within a reasonable period.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We may update this policy as the service evolves. Material changes will
          be posted here with a new date; continued use after a change means you
          accept the updated policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</.page_shell>
